  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f7987a5c-3182-5f7a-9e88-aee3156fcd3a" activityNameId="3cd56403-fb85-5c51-af84-5f4ed19456aa" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production DZ, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production DZ, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 81% of the imported Algerian natural gas to GLO was imported by pipeline and 19% as LNG. An average distance of 1910 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Algeria, of which are 140 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are 6800 km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=c4f4f8b3-6c3c-3ff3-8124-8d7a14069e6f
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Algerian natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_c4f4f8b3-6c3c-3ff3-8124-8d7a14069e6f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
